INTERPRETATION
--------------
Adding Taylor to either proxy improves RMSE, MAE, Pearson and R2 relative to that proxy alone under the unadjusted intervals. Spearman improvements remain inconclusive.
Taylor+SynFlow is worse than Taylor alone on RMSE, MAE, Pearson and R2 under the intervals; Spearman is inconclusive.
Taylor+NASWOT improves RMSE, MAE and R2 versus Taylor alone, but worsens Pearson; Spearman is inconclusive.
Taylor+NASWOT has the lowest point-estimate errors among these five calibrators; Taylor alone has the highest correlations. All R2 values remain negative.

